# CI's fresh, proxyless runner address consistently gets dd.solve.failed /
# Access Denied from these where the same commits solve locally — kept
# locally for reference, not committed until that's understood.
#
# grainger-lightpanda and comcast-lightpanda came back on 2026-09-26, now that
# src/mitm.ts puts Chrome's real ClientHello and HTTP/2 SETTINGS on the wire.
# comcast solves consistently; grainger solves at the rate its own header
# documents, about one run in two or three, which is DataDome scoring a solve
# computed from a Lightpanda page and not the address. Both are advisory in the
# smoke suite, so CI reports them without gating on any of it.
